    <section id="about" class="section wrap split-section"><div class="section-kicker">01 / The premise</div><div class="section-content"><h2>Markets are changing.<br><span>So must our models.</span></h2><div class="body-grid"><p class="large-copy">Artificial intelligence is reshaping how financial markets are designed, analyzed and operated. New venues, new assets and new forms of automation are opening questions that sit at the frontier of market microstructure.</p><div><p>From centralized exchanges to decentralized protocols, trading, liquidity provision, price formation and information flow remain central challenges. This workshop brings the communities working on these questions into the same room.</p><p>Through invited talks, contributed presentations, panels and interactive sessions, we will explore how machine learning, reinforcement learning, agent-based modelling and data-driven methods can improve our understanding of modern financial systems.</p></div></div></div></section>

    <section id="topics" class="section topics-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-kicker">02 / Open questions</div><h2>What are you<br><span>working on?</span></h2><div class="topic-grid"><article><small>01</small><h3>AI agents<br>for trading</h3><p>Learning, reasoning and acting in complex market environments.</p></article><article><small>02</small><h3>Liquidity &amp;<br>market making</h3><p>How intelligent agents provide and consume liquidity.</p></article><article><small>03</small><h3>Price discovery<br>&amp; execution</h3><p>New methods for routing, forecasting and optimal execution.</p></article><article><small>04</small><h3>DeFi<br>microstructure</h3><p>AMMs, order books, MEV, protocols and tokenized assets.</p></article><article><small>05</small><h3>Risk, design<br>&amp; regulation</h3><p>Robustness, surveillance and the governance of AI in markets.</p></article></div></div></section>

    <section id="dates" class="section wrap timeline-section"><div class="section-kicker">03 / Important dates</div><div class="timeline"><div><span class="date">TBC</span><h3>Abstract deadline</h3><p>Deadline for workshop abstract submissions.</p></div><div><span class="date">TBC</span><h3>Notification of acceptance</h3><p>Authors will be notified about the outcome of their submission.</p></div><div><span class="date">14—17 NOV 2026</span><h3>ICAIF '26 · Milan</h3><p>The workshop takes place during ICAIF at Bocconi University.</p></div></div></section>

